# `AxumAppBuilder`

<SymbolMeta />
<SymbolSignature />

`AxumAppBuilder` is the extension trait that adds Axum-specific methods to `AppBuilder<Axum>`. It is available from the facade prelude. Its WebSocket methods are the endpoint boundary: controllers declare which protocol they speak, while this trait selects the upgrade path and options that activate it.

```rust
use upwell::prelude::*;
use upwell::axum::prelude::*;

let app = App::builder("chat")
    .register_ws::<JsonWs>("/ws")
    .register_ws_with::<Stomp>("/stomp", StompConfig::default())
    .build()
    .await?;
```

`register_ws` uses `P::Options::default()`. `register_ws_with` accepts explicit options for one mount. Both register `P`, collect only `#[controller(ws = P)]` descriptors, call `P::build` during application construction, and mount the generic upgrade handler at the given absolute path. A protocol may have multiple mounts at distinct paths; duplicate WebSocket paths are rejected during preparation.

Use `controller::<T>()` for explicit HTTP controller registration and `middleware` or `layer` for application middleware. Those methods do not replace WebSocket registration: an HTTP controller path is not a WebSocket upgrade endpoint.

